        <a href="threat-center.html">Threat Center</a>
        <a href="about.html">About</a>
        <a href="contact.html" class="nav-cta">Book Assessment</a>
      </nav>

      <button class="menu-toggle" id="menuToggle" aria-label="Toggle menu">☰</button>
    </div>

    <div class="mobile-nav" id="mobileNav">
      <a href="index.html">Home</a>
      <a href="services.html">Services</a>
      <a href="future-tech.html">Future Tech</a>
      <a href="threat-center.html">Threat Center</a>
      <a href="about.html">About</a>
      <a href="contact.html">Book Assessment</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="future-hero">
      <div class="future-particles"></div>

      <div class="container">
        <div class="future-hero-grid">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">FUTURE TECH</p>
            <h1>Blossom is the long-term vision behind smarter Lotus security operations</h1>
            <p class="future-copy">
              Blossom represents the future-facing side of Lotus: better visibility, better prioritization,
              cleaner client reporting, and more intelligent support for defensive operations without losing
              human judgment, context, or accountability.
            </p>

            <div class="future-pill">
              <span>Status:</span>
              <strong>Vision in Development</strong>
            </div>

            <div class="future-actions">
              <a href="contact.html" class="btn btn-primary">Work With Lotus</a>
              <a href="threat-center.html" class="btn btn-secondary">View Threat Center</a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="future-visual">
            <div class="glass glow-border future-image-shell">
              <div class="future-overlay-top">
                <strong>Blossom</strong>
                <span>AI-assisted security vision</span>
              </div>

              <img src="blossom-hero.png" alt="Blossom futuristic graphic" class="future-image" />

              <div class="future-overlay-bottom">
                <strong>Purpose</strong>
                <span>Support visibility, triage, reporting, and smarter defensive workflows</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section alt-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">WHAT BLOSSOM STANDS FOR</p>
          <h2>Not a gimmick. Not a chatbot with a pretty face. A future operating layer.</h2>
          <p>
            Blossom is meant to represent a more intelligent layer around Lotus services: something that helps sort signal from noise,
            improve client understanding, and make security operations feel cleaner, faster, and more usable.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="future-section-grid">
          <div class="glass future-card">
            <h3>Threat Visibility</h3>
            <p>
              Surface the activity that actually matters and reduce blind spots across business environments that usually lack dedicated security teams.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="glass future-card">
            <h3>Alert Prioritization</h3>
            <p>
              Help direct attention toward the events, weaknesses, and changes that deserve action instead of drowning in background noise.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="glass future-card">
            <h3>Client Intelligence</h3>
            <p>
              Turn technical security data into cleaner, easier-to-understand reporting that helps clients see what Lotus is protecting and why it matters.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="future-roadmap">
          <div class="glass roadmap-story">
            <p class="eyebrow">ROADMAP</p>
            <h2>Blossom fits into the future of Lotus, not outside of it</h2>
            <p>
              Lotus is being built as a real-world security company first. That means assessments, hardening, client guidance,
              recurring protection, and disciplined service structure come before flashy promises. Blossom sits on top of that
              foundation as the future-facing layer that can make the whole system smarter.
            </p>
            <p>
              The long-term idea is not to replace people. It is to give Lotus and its clients better visibility into risk,
              faster awareness around what changed, and a cleaner way to understand where security effort is going.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="glass roadmap-points">
            <p class="eyebrow">POTENTIAL CAPABILITIES</p>
            <h2>What that future could look like</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>Client-facing visibility into environment status and security posture</li>
              <li>Smarter prioritization of findings and recurring risks</li>
              <li>Cleaner reporting that shows what changed over time</li>
              <li>Better translation of technical issues into business meaning</li>
              <li>AI-assisted workflows that support, not replace, human security judgment</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section alt-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">THE RIGHT FRAME</p>
          <h2>How Lotus sees AI in security</h2>
          <p>
            The point is not to pretend AI solves cybersecurity by itself. The point is to use intelligent systems where they help,
            keep humans where they are needed, and avoid building trust on hype.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="future-comparison">
          <div class="glass compare-box">
            <h3>What Blossom is not</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>A replacement for real security work</li>
              <li>A fake promise of fully automated defense</li>
              <li>A gimmick meant to distract from service quality</li>
              <li>A vague marketing mascot with no purpose</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="glass compare-box">
            <h3>What Blossom is meant to become</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>A future-facing support layer around Lotus operations</li>
              <li>A cleaner way to communicate risk and protection to clients</li>
              <li>A tool for better triage, visibility, and prioritization</li>
              <li>A premium expression of where Lotus is headed</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="glass future-cta">
          <p class="eyebrow">LOOKING AHEAD</p>
          <h2>Lotus is built for real protection now and smarter operations later</h2>
          <p>
            Blossom represents the future side of that mission: intelligent support, better visibility, stronger communication,
            and a cleaner security experience layered on top of real-world service.
          </p>

          <div style="display:flex; gap:14px; justify-content:center; flex-wrap:wrap;">
            <a href="contact.html" class="btn btn-primary">Talk to Lotus</a>
            <a href="about.html" class="btn btn-secondary">Why Lotus Exists</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

